WEBVTT

00:00:00.638 --> 00:00:04.432
This guide explains the optional Companion firmware what it is

00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:07.058
for what it does not do and how to install

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.370
it safely in your browser

00:00:10.262 --> 00:00:14.982
The round Waveshare device contains two independent processors The E

00:00:14.875 --> 00:00:19.232
S P thirty-two S three runs RoonPilot including the display

00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:23.808
touch controls rotary control and network connection The second

00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:27.920
classic E S P thirty-two is the companion processor It

00:00:27.812 --> 00:00:31.045
is inside the same device not a separate Bridge

00:00:32.946 --> 00:00:37.141
RoonPilot does not need the second processor The small Sleep

00:00:37.033 --> 00:00:41.028
firmware mutes its unused audio output leaves the shared signal

00:00:40.921 --> 00:00:45.078
lines inactive and puts the companion processor into indefinite deep

00:00:44.971 --> 00:00:49.528
sleep This avoids unnecessary activity and is intended to save

00:00:49.421 --> 00:00:50.041
power

00:00:51.904 --> 00:00:55.024
It does not turn RoonPilot into a music player or

00:00:54.917 --> 00:00:58.312
a Roon audio endpoint It does not extend an I

00:00:58.204 --> 00:01:00.862
R or R M E Bridge and it does not

00:01:00.754 --> 00:01:05.287
replace undervoltage protection The audio D A C mentioned here

00:01:05.179 --> 00:01:07.974
is the small chip on the Waveshare board not your

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.174
external R M E D A C

00:01:12.029 --> 00:01:16.899
This installation is optional RoonPilot works fully without it

00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:22.549
Afterwards the display touch controls rotary control Wi-Fi and Roon

00:01:22.442 --> 00:01:26.387
connection still work Deep sleep affects only the companion

00:01:26.279 --> 00:01:31.124
processor not RoonPilot No particular increase in battery life is

00:01:31.017 --> 00:01:34.412
promised other parts of the board still consume power

00:01:36.346 --> 00:01:39.378
You need a computer a U S B data cable

00:01:39.558 --> 00:01:42.728
and a current Chrome or Edge browser On a Mac

00:01:42.896 --> 00:01:46.791
you can use Chrome Safari and Firefox cannot run this

00:01:46.683 --> 00:01:50.541
U S B installer Close other programs using a serial

00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:54.128
U S B connection and connect RoonPilot directly to the

00:01:54.021 --> 00:01:54.778
computer

00:01:56.654 --> 00:02:01.124
Only the companion processor's firmware is erased and replaced The

00:02:01.017 --> 00:02:05.799
RoonPilot version Wi-Fi settings profiles and Bridge pairings on the

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:09.562
main processor remain unchanged If you may want the exact

00:02:09.454 --> 00:02:13.787
original Waveshare companion firmware back later save it first using

00:02:13.679 --> 00:02:17.362
the linked guide That backup is not required for normal

00:02:17.254 --> 00:02:18.237
installation

00:02:20.112 --> 00:02:23.970
Open the address shown here in your browser Companion at

00:02:23.862 --> 00:02:27.220
the end of the address is important You can also

00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:30.558
choose Open the Companion Web Installer on the main installer

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:34.432
page The heading should say Companion Firmware Installer

00:02:36.308 --> 00:02:41.053
Scroll to Install Companion Sleep This shows the separate Companion

00:02:40.946 --> 00:02:44.791
version one point zero point one in this example It

00:02:44.683 --> 00:02:48.728
is not an older RoonPilot version Each processor has its

00:02:48.621 --> 00:02:50.603
own firmware and version number

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.220
Read the notice about selecting the right processor and replacing

00:02:56.112 --> 00:03:00.695
its firmware Read the licence as well Tick both boxes

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:05.358
Only then does Install Companion firmware become available Click it

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:07.495
to open the device selection window

00:03:09.417 --> 00:03:13.574
For this installation U S B serial is correct On

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:16.524
Windows it has a C O M number On a

00:03:16.417 --> 00:03:19.824
Mac the port name may contain c u dot usbserial

00:03:19.917 --> 00:03:24.949
or wchusbserial These endings are only examples The device name

00:03:24.842 --> 00:03:28.762
is what matters If it already appears select it and

00:03:28.654 --> 00:03:29.399
connect

00:03:31.304 --> 00:03:34.212
If you see U S B J tag serial debug

00:03:34.104 --> 00:03:37.924
unit instead you are connected to the main processor This

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:41.224
is the wrong side for the Companion firmware Do not

00:03:41.117 --> 00:03:45.024
select it Leave the device selection window open and turn

00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:46.699
the connector as shown next

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:52.820
Unplug the U S B C connector at RoonPilot Leave

00:03:52.712 --> 00:03:56.758
the other end connected to your computer The existing entry

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:00.408
disappears from the list You do not need another socket

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:01.432
or another cable

00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:06.553
Rotate the connector around its own length by one hundred

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:09.841
and eighty degrees The side that was facing up now

00:04:09.733 --> 00:04:14.566
faces down On this board the connector orientation determines which

00:04:14.458 --> 00:04:17.203
processor is accessible over U S B

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:22.545
Plug the cable back into the same socket The list

00:04:22.438 --> 00:04:26.470
updates and U S B serial should now appear Select

00:04:26.362 --> 00:04:30.032
that entry then click Connect You only need to turn

00:04:29.925 --> 00:04:32.558
the connector if the wrong name was shown before

00:04:34.446 --> 00:04:39.091
In the small window choose Install RoonPilot Companion Sleep The

00:04:38.983 --> 00:04:42.928
installer dialogs are in English You do not need Logs

00:04:42.821 --> 00:04:45.166
and Console for a normal installation

00:04:47.071 --> 00:04:50.803
The Erase device window now appears Tick the box to

00:04:50.696 --> 00:04:54.016
erase the companion processor's memory completely before

00:04:53.908 --> 00:04:58.728
installation Then click Next This warning refers only to the

00:04:58.621 --> 00:05:02.616
selected companion processor not to your RoonPilot settings

00:05:04.475 --> 00:05:08.708
Check that the confirmation window names RoonPilot Companion Sleep

00:05:08.988 --> 00:05:12.932
The erase warning still refers only to this processor If

00:05:12.825 --> 00:05:17.258
everything is correct click Install The firmware is now written

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.195
to the device

00:05:20.083 --> 00:05:24.291
The installer prepares the installation erases the memory and writes

00:05:24.183 --> 00:05:28.891
the firmware The percentage shows progress It then finishes the

00:05:28.783 --> 00:05:33.103
process Keep this window visible and do not disconnect U

00:05:32.996 --> 00:05:37.578
S B The video shortens this sequence your installation may

00:05:37.471 --> 00:05:38.378
take longer

00:05:40.304 --> 00:05:44.637
Wait for Installation complete Only then is the installation

00:05:44.529 --> 00:05:48.787
finished Click Next and close the small window Do not

00:05:48.679 --> 00:05:52.362
unplug just because the progress reaches one hundred percent while

00:05:52.254 --> 00:05:53.949
Wrapping up is still displayed

00:05:55.833 --> 00:05:59.353
There is no setup Wi-Fi no separate website and no

00:05:59.246 --> 00:06:03.128
Roon authorisation for the Companion firmware Its job is to

00:06:03.021 --> 00:06:06.666
go to sleep after starting Whenever the device is powered

00:06:06.558 --> 00:06:10.903
on again the companion processor returns to this power-saving state

00:06:12.779 --> 00:06:15.887
Now return the cable to the orientation for the main

00:06:15.779 --> 00:06:20.099
processor After the successful installation unplug it at the

00:06:19.992 --> 00:06:24.724
RoonPilot end The Companion firmware remains stored permanently

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:29.707
Turn the connector over by another one hundred and eighty

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:34.382
degrees The opposite side faces up again This returns you

00:06:34.275 --> 00:06:36.857
to the normal U S B connection with the main

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:37.557
processor

00:06:39.446 --> 00:06:42.966
Plug the cable back in and wait for RoonPilot The

00:06:42.858 --> 00:06:45.566
normal U S B side is now U S B

00:06:45.458 --> 00:06:48.991
J tag serial debug unit again You do not need

00:06:48.883 --> 00:06:53.053
to install anything there Companion Sleep and the main firmware

00:06:52.946 --> 00:06:54.778
are now present independently

00:06:56.679 --> 00:07:00.987
If RoonPilot was already configured it continues using its existing

00:07:00.879 --> 00:07:04.499
settings You do not need to set up Wi-Fi Roon

00:07:04.479 --> 00:07:07.837
or Bridges again because of Companion Sleep If the main

00:07:07.729 --> 00:07:11.824
firmware was not installed yet also follow our regular RoonPilot

00:07:11.717 --> 00:07:16.012
video guide This Companion installation does not replace it

00:07:17.929 --> 00:07:20.862
If the list is empty check the data cable and

00:07:20.754 --> 00:07:24.762
close other serial programs If the E S P thirty-two

00:07:24.654 --> 00:07:28.774
S three is reported as unsupported close the dialog turn

00:07:28.667 --> 00:07:32.462
the connector and reconnect to the Companion side After an

00:07:32.354 --> 00:07:36.824
interrupted installation run the same Companion installer again Do

00:07:36.717 --> 00:07:38.899
not substitute the main firmware

00:07:40.779 --> 00:07:45.562
All done The companion processor sleeps while RoonPilot remains your

00:07:45.454 --> 00:07:49.149
remote control All steps and links to the written guide

00:07:49.042 --> 00:07:52.699
are below this video Take your time and repeat any

00:07:52.592 --> 00:07:53.674
chapter you need
